*****************************************************************************/
    A form file is definitions only: loading it draws nothing. To fire one, put its lines in tester above the SENTINEL line, after tester's own
    Start() and includes. One form at a time. This heading is the only home for these lines (Tony, 2026-11-13). To look: open -a Skim IncantForms/PDF/output.pdf
    firstLight:
        registry(fILEs);
        define
            firstLightFile File='IncantForms/Windows/firstLight';
            ;
        include(styles);
        search cOLOr fONTs sTYLEs;
        include(firstLightFile);
        search FORMs UnitTests Utilities cOLOr fONTs sTYLEs list;
        define
            flReq path="IncantForms/PDF/output.pdf" form:=firstLight;
            ;
        redrawForm(flReq);
    descriptions: the same lines with descriptionsFile File='IncantForms/Windows/descriptions' and include(descriptionsFile); its request is descriptionsReq path="IncantForms/PDF/output.pdf" form:=descriptions; and its call redrawForm(descriptionsReq);
